Most warlocks use voidwalkers in Classic WoW not because they're better for leveling or questing, but because **voidwalkers are more effective in group content and dungeons**—especially for threat generation and survivability. While succubuses are excellent for soloing and stealthy questing, they lack strong threat and utility in group settings. Voidwalkers provide reliable taunt, threat, and survivability, making them more practical for group dynamics, especially in dungeons and raids. Thus, they're more commonly seen in group play, even if succubuses are better for solo progression. [end of text]


